      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Altogether 123 angina patients were examined using electrocardiography and scintigraphy of the myocardium with two 99m Tc radiopharmaceutical complexes: pyrophosphate and phosphone. A comparative analysis of the results obtained with different methods of investigation before and after an attack of angina pectoris was made. The authors have shown some peculiarities of radionuclide distribution in the myocardium and the diagnostic value of each method of investigation in patients with different clinical forms of angina pectoris."},
